{{!--
  WHAT A CREATURE IS CARRYING (the lead's N3, 2026-09-10).

  The character's Gear tab, minus two things the lead ruled out: **containers**
  (`gear.hbs`'s `{{#each containers}}` sections and every `data-container-id`
  drop zone) and **the paper doll** (every `data-slot` control, which lives on
  the character's Overview tab and never on this one). What is left is the same
  rows through the same partial, the same carry line and the same purse.

  The rows are still `draggable` — that is `carried-row.hbs`'s own class and
  core's drag selector — but there is no zone on this tab for a drag to land
  in, so a drop inside the list falls through to core's sort exactly as it does
  on every untabbed surface.
--}}
<section class="tab azeroth-panel {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="gear" data-group="primary">
  <h3 class="azeroth-panel-heading">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.Carried"}}</h3>
  {{!-- What it is carrying against what it can (05 SS10, 08 SS11; D-675).
        **A `—` STRENGTH HAS NO LIMIT** (14 SS1 prints the dash and `NpcData`
        keeps it null): there is no denominator, so there is no bar and the
        count says so in words rather than reading `12 / 0 lb`. --}}
  <div class="azeroth-load is-{{load.state}}">
    <div class="azeroth-load-head">
      <span class="azeroth-load-label">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.CarryCapacity"}}</span>
      {{#if load.unlimited}}
      <span class="azeroth-load-count">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.CarriedNoLimit" used=load.carried}}</span>
      {{else}}
      <span class="azeroth-load-count">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.CarriedOf" used=load.carried max=load.capacity}}</span>
      {{/if}}
      {{#if load.penalty}}<span class="azeroth-load-state">{{localize load.label}} &middot; {{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.LoadPenalty" n=load.penalty}}</span>{{/if}}
      {{!-- The purse in copper (08 SS2's coin, D-422), printed as the chapter
            prints it. 14 states no purse: what a creature is carrying is a
            world-level GM act, which is why the bestiary pack gains nothing. --}}
      <span class="azeroth-purse">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.Purse"}}: <span class="azeroth-purse-coins">{{purse}}</span>{{#if editable}} <input type="number" name="system.coin" value="{{system.coin}}" min="0" step="1" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.PurseCopper"}}"> {{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.Copper"}}{{/if}}</span>
    </div>
    {{#unless load.unlimited}}
    <div class="azeroth-load-track" role="img" aria-label="{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.CarriedOf" used=load.carried max=load.capacity}}">
      <span class="azeroth-load-fill" style="width: {{load.percent}}%"></span>
    </div>
    {{/unless}}
  </div>

  {{!-- 08 SS9 locks an Augment to a class and a creature holds no class item,
        so nothing refuses one here. Said in words rather than left silent. --}}
  {{#if augmentNote}}<p class="azeroth-note azeroth-augment-note">{{augmentNote}}</p>{{/if}}

  {{#if carried}}
  {{#each carriedGroups as |group|}}
  <h4 class="azeroth-gear-heading">{{localize group.label}}</h4>
  <ol class="azeroth-carried">
    {{#each group.items as |row|}}
    {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/carried-row.hbs row=row editable=@root.editable}}
    {{/each}}
  </ol>
  {{/each}}
  {{else}}
  <p class="azeroth-note">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.NothingCarried"}}</p>
  {{/if}}

  {{!-- Add opens the compendium browser on the kind; a GM's right click on the
        button makes a blank one instead (`blankItemMenu`). --}}
  <div class="azeroth-add-row">
    <button type="button" data-action="browseItems" data-type="weapon">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.AddWeapon"}}</button>
    <button type="button" data-action="browseItems" data-type="armor">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.AddArmor"}}</button>
    <button type="button" data-action="browseItems" data-type="gear">{{localize "AZEROTH.Sheet.AddGear"}}</button>
  </div>
</section>
